resources/python
resources/python_aarch64

*storybook.log
node_modules

# The built Storybook. `pnpm build-storybook` writes it so a capture run can be
# served from a static tree rather than a dev server, which is the cheap way to
# capture on a loaded machine. It is a build artifact of `src/` - nothing reads
# it, `capture-evidence.mjs` takes an origin and does not care how it is served,
# and committing it put 327 files and ~67k lines of vendored bundle in a docs
# commit (review round 3, MAJOR 1).
storybook-static/
